concat_ws.usage:
Function: concat_ws
Class: org.apache.spark.sql.catalyst.expressions.ConcatWs
Usage: concat_ws(sep[, str | array(str)]+) - Returns the concatenation of the strings separated by `sep`, skipping null values.
Extended Usage:
    Examples:
      > SELECT concat_ws(' ', 'Spark', 'SQL');
        Spark SQL
      > SELECT concat_ws('s');

      > SELECT concat_ws('/', 'foo', null, 'bar');
        foo/bar
      > SELECT concat_ws(null, 'Spark', 'SQL');
        NULL

    Since: 1.5.0

exists.usage:
Function: exists
Class: org.apache.spark.sql.catalyst.expressions.ArrayExists
Usage: exists(expr, pred) - Tests whether a predicate holds for one or more elements in the array.
Extended Usage:
    Examples:
      > SELECT exists(array(1, 2, 3), x -> x % 2 == 0);
       true
      > SELECT exists(array(1, 2, 3), x -> x % 2 == 10);
       false
      > SELECT exists(array(1, null, 3), x -> x % 2 == 0);
       NULL
      > SELECT exists(array(0, null, 2, 3, null), x -> x IS NULL);
       true
      > SELECT exists(array(1, 2, 3), x -> x IS NULL);
       false

    Since: 2.4.0

from_csv.usage:
Function: from_csv
Class: org.apache.spark.sql.catalyst.expressions.CsvToStructs
Usage: from_csv(csvStr, schema[, options]) - Returns a struct value with the given `csvStr` and `schema`.
Extended Usage:
    Examples:
      > SELECT from_csv('1, 0.8', 'a INT, b DOUBLE');
       {"a":1,"b":0.8}
      > SELECT from_csv('26/08/2015', 'time Timestamp', map('timestampFormat', 'dd/MM/yyyy'));
       {"time":2015-08-26 00:00:00}

    Since: 3.0.0

from_json.usage:
Function: from_json
Class: org.apache.spark.sql.catalyst.expressions.JsonToStructs
Usage: from_json(jsonStr, schema[, options]) - Returns a struct value with the given `jsonStr` and `schema`.
